    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Atlas publishes no releases and every build reports the same version string (spark 1.0.0-beta-preview), so the engine version registered for this run is the git commit, as the sparkinfer entry does. engine.build carries Atlas-Inf/atlas@bdcccc2c."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "The published container azeezish/atlas-gb10:latest (digest sha256:faa6e5820c42dd86d0ae9e12cbaf2a2e9f32d0f7a9ab348a75ee54d4253929a6) CANNOT run these recipes: its spark serve --help has no --prefill-varlen-batch and its --ssm-h-dtype accepts only f32 and f16, not f16-pool. Both landed in Atlas-Inf/atlas#572 on 2026-08-18 and the image predates them despite a later tag date. This run is therefore a source build, not that image."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "The engine will not link with default cargo features: NCCL is a default feature and libnccl is absent on a single-box DGX Spark. Build with --no-default-features --features cuda."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "spark serve --check-kernels is a real preflight and worth running first: it loads the model, resolves every kernel lookup and exits with the number that did not resolve. Here it reported 251 lookups, 0 unresolved, 1 expected-absent for (qwen3.8-27b, sm_121, nvfp4), kernel_set_hash 7d4320ea200f. An unresolved lookup does not error at serve time - it silently takes a slower dispatch path."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Four of this configuration's knobs have no CLI flag and are read from the environment (ATLAS_PREFILL_CODISPATCH, ATLAS_FP8_ROWWISE, ATLAS_MTP_DCUT_RATIO, ATLAS_MTP_K_LADDER). The published recipe says the ladder does not reproduce without them, so they are registered as engine params and passed in args; a fingerprint that dropped them would merge two configurations that differ by more than 20% at C=2."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Configuration is the published recipe Atlas-Inf/sparkrun-recipes recipes/qwen3.8/qwen3.8-27b-nvfp4-latency.yaml verbatim. Its max_model_len is 32768 - the recipe's own honest ceiling, because the kernel target declares effective_context 24576 - not the 262144 the weights nominally support, so the 65536/131072/262144 points of the long-context sweep are recorded as context-overflow failures."
    }
